+# Orch v4.7.14 installation and acceptance candidate
 
-Only PO downloads and installs. Install under ~/SW_Dev/rwt-pr-handoff-v4.7.13 using the same gh blob download, checksum verification, unzip and python3 orch-setup.py flow as v4.7.11. It starts in this terminal and opens http://127.0.0.1:4317/ after the actual API confirms version 4.7.13. Keep the terminal running. No LaunchAgent or login service is installed.
+Build: coordination.8-work. This candidate is installable, but automatic idle wake, legacy watcher restoration and stuck-delivery recovery are NOT accepted on the Mac. It is not a release receipt or a claim that copy-paste is eliminated. Keep the v4.7.13 installation intact.
 
-Before upgrading, stop the old foreground board with Ctrl-C in its terminal when no worker action is in flight. The installer preserves a running board instead of killing active work, explicitly reports an old version, and does not pretend the upgrade occurred. Run the installation block in any directory; it changes into the extracted absolute folder itself.
+## Install using the established foreground flow
 
-On a fresh v4.7.13 folder, automatically prefer a verified v4.7.12 migration journal, then v4.7.11, then verified v4.7.10, then the known v4.7.7-candidate source. Preserve database, private pairing and artifacts. Existing target state and an explicit migration override are retained; unknown ambiguous history is not guessed. Original installations remain intact.
+Only the Product Owner downloads this ZIP. Devs do not install Orch. Existing Python 3.10+, gh and Codex logins are reused. No LaunchAgent or login service is installed.
 
-Existing gh/Codex login and paired routes remain prerequisites, not repeated setup. First launch announces the new app version through the supported routes and requires real recipient receipts/results. Devs do not install this bundle. Native CLI PM receives current events in its PM queue; an unsupported browser chat cannot be automatically awakened. A stale/unrearmed listener remains an explicit transport blocker, never a fabricated ACK.
+1. Download rwt-pr-handoff-v4.7.14-candidate.zip to ~/Downloads.
+2. When the old board and its workers are idle, stop its foreground terminal with Ctrl-C. A running old board is preserved by setup; the candidate will not kill it or pretend it upgraded.
+3. If ~/SW_Dev/rwt-pr-handoff-v4.7.14 already exists, preserve it and inspect it before extracting; do not overwrite private state or merge two package versions.
+4. In Terminal, run:
 
-Accept the installed upgrade only after the board reports 4.7.13 coordination.7, then a real current CI/review event reaches CLI PM and the intended Dev, with authenticated receipt/result and PM follow-through without PO relay. Offline tests do not substitute for this host proof.
+```bash
+mkdir -p "$HOME/SW_Dev"
+unzip -n "$HOME/Downloads/rwt-pr-handoff-v4.7.14-candidate.zip" -d "$HOME/SW_Dev"
+cd "$HOME/SW_Dev/rwt-pr-handoff-v4.7.14"
+python3 orch-setup.py
+```
+
+Keep this terminal running. Setup validates the manifest, reuses existing logins and routes, migrates verified state, starts in the foreground and opens http://127.0.0.1:4317/ after the actual API reports v4.7.14. Later starts use the same python3 orch-setup.py command, or Start_Orch.command from this installed folder.
+
+## State and agent setup
+
+A fresh target prefers the completed, verified v4.7.13 migration journal, then verified v4.7.12/11/10/7.7-candidate. Existing target state and an explicit migration override are preserved. Database, receipts/cursor/dedupe, private routes and artifacts are copied without altering the source installation. Missing or ambiguous provenance is a hold; do not reset agents to get around it.
+
+Recipient pairing UI has been removed. CLI PM owns nonce-bound identity negotiation on launch and recovery. This reuses existing supported routes; it does not silently invent a missing app-server connection, restore a Claude tracked task by detached polling, or grant a browser chat an unsupported inbound wake. An identity ACK is separate from a real idle wake/receipt/result.
+
+## Accept or hold
+
+Confirm the board reports v4.7.14 / coordination.8-work, expected prior tasks/receipts and read-only agent diagnostics. A real PM event must wake the verified idle recipient, produce matching authenticated receipt/result and survive an idle foreground restart without duplicate execution. Mac sleep/resume and compaction/watcher restoration remain required. A poll-only/blocked/uncertain route is HOLD, not connected proof.
+
+Known open work: real idle delivery; automatic legacy tracked-watcher restoration; stuck-route/owned-process cleanup reconciliation; dependency-aware CI qualification as a separate repository increment. The bounded Codex summary-read correction is tested locally, but recovery2160's Mac cause is not established.
+
+To return to v4.7.13, first settle or reconcile any candidate action and stop the candidate when idle, then run python3 orch-setup.py in the retained v4.7.13 folder. Its old state is preserved; new candidate receipts are not automatically reverse-migrated. Do not run both boards or replay uncertain tasks.
